  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of elevation of the summit of a mountain from a point on the ground is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. After climbing up one km towards the summit at an inclination of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;from the ground, the angle of elevation of the summit is found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Then the height (in km) of the summit from the ground is :"
